## Limitations and B4 boundary

New rejection record append/load and `_publish` union branches are statically reviewed, not executed. The historical evaluated load proves only legacy compatibility. No fabricated case was used to claim stronger coverage.

The new event-reference check uses exact canonical integer formatting, including values wider than the minimum widths. Existing `load_round_events` still accepts only six-digit sequence filenames; this inherited B2 limit is unchanged and would fail closed for sequences above 999999. No journal format/replay change was made in B3b.

`_verify_finalized_discovery_rounds` still compares candidate IDs with rendered_variant-only IDs and requires investigator/author/critic completion. `_completed_result` and recovery retain critic assumptions. B4 must support legitimate rejection-inclusive/rejection-only closure while preserving all authority checks and mandatory critic for testable records. Strict rendering activation, `no_testable_experiments`, critic requests, completion/recovery, cleanup and feedback remain untouched. This checkpoint does not claim that the end-to-end rejected lifecycle works, and does not complete either outstanding evaluated feedback round.
